1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,376
This proof of concept shows how coverage becomes a reviewed briefing.

2
00:00:04,376 --> 00:00:05,859
The data is synthetic.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,356
It starts with the client brief and three approved key messages.

4
00:00:12,356 --> 00:00:17,109
Then sixteen articles of coverage, with duplicates and incomplete records set aside.

5
00:00:19,899 --> 00:00:22,846
Next, a rules based analysis labels each article.

6
00:00:22,846 --> 00:00:28,002
It is not a language model, so it behaves the same way every run.

7
00:00:28,002 --> 00:00:35,000
Every finding shows the exact quote behind it, and the app checks that quote really appears in the article.

8
00:00:37,299 --> 00:00:38,727
Then people take over.

9
00:00:38,727 --> 00:00:44,794
A reviewer accepts, corrects or rejects every finding, and the briefing stays locked until that is done.

10
00:00:44,794 --> 00:00:49,077
Every action is logged with who made it, when, and what changed.

11
00:00:49,077 --> 00:00:52,289
The reviewer picker is fictional, not real sign in.

12
00:01:00,299 --> 00:01:04,428
Once the review is complete, the numbers are for the client.

13
00:01:04,428 --> 00:01:10,810
Message penetration and tone are calculated only from the reviewed set, and they are labelled as illustrative.

14
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,586
Here is the advisory panel.

15
00:01:14,586 --> 00:01:17,226
It is simulated, not four AI agents.

16
00:01:17,226 --> 00:01:24,017
Four rule based perspectives read the same reviewed results and apply different fixed rules, so they can disagree.

17
00:01:24,017 --> 00:01:30,430
Each point is marked supported, assumption, or not enough evidence, and then a synthesis pulls it together.

18
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,302
Finally, Ask the Campaign.

19
00:01:42,302 --> 00:01:48,166
A suggested question gets an answer built from the reviewed data, with a link back to the evidence.

20
00:01:48,166 --> 00:01:50,446
I can also type my own question.

21
00:01:50,446 --> 00:01:56,310
It is matched to supported topics by simple rules, so it is a guided demo, not a chatbot.

22
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,439
The goal is simple: AI that helps, with people in control and every decision on record.

23
00:02:16,439 --> 00:02:17,120
Thank you.
